### ==============================================================================
### User Management CRUD API Test Suite
### Compatible with both ASP.NET Core (port 5000) and Golang Gin (port 8080)
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
# Switch to Gin by toggling the comment:
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Retrieve all users (Initially empty)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

### 2. Create a User - Failure (Validation error: missing FirstName and invalid email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "invalid-email-address"
}

### 3. Create User 1 - Success (201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com"
}

### 4. Create User 2 - Success (201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com"
}

### 5. Create User - Failure (Duplicate Email Conflict - 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com"
}

### 6. Retrieve all users (Should contain 2 users)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

### 7. Retrieve single user by ID (200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Accept: application/json

### 8. Retrieve non-existent user by ID (404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/999
Accept: application/json

### 9. Update existing user (200 OK)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Johnathan",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "johnathan.updated@example.com"
}

### 10. Update user with conflicting email (409 Conflict)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Johnathan",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com"
}

### 11. Delete user by ID (204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1

### 12. Retrieve deleted user (404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Accept: application/json
